# #1284: this is the file Docker ACTUALLY reads for apps/file-manager's build
# (the CLI's `requireBuildContext` resolves the build context to the
# workspace ROOT — where a lockfile marker is found above the app — so the
# per-app apps/file-manager/.dockerignore is NOT the file that gates
# `docker build`'s context here; this one is). `.vinext/fonts/<hash>/style.css`
# caches a self-hosted next/font/google file by an ABSOLUTE FILESYSTEM PATH
# computed at fetch time (vinext's createGoogleFontsPlugin). `kn-next deploy`/
# `kn-next build` run the app's own `vite build` on the HOST before the Docker
# build; without this exclusion that HOST-path cache rides `COPY . .` into the
# image, and the in-image `RUN vite build` (apps/file-manager/Dockerfile) hits
# a CACHE HIT on the stale style.css — vinext returns it verbatim, and its
# rewrite-to-a-served-URL step only fires when the cached path matches the
# CURRENT build's cacheDir, so the HOST path leaks straight into the served
# page.
#
# MUST be `**/.vinext`, not a bare `.vinext`. Unlike `.gitignore`, a bare
# `.dockerignore` pattern matches ONLY at the context root — it does NOT
# recurse into subdirectories the way a bare gitignore pattern does. Proved
# with a minimal reproduction (a nested `subdir/.vinext/` survived a bare
# `.vinext` line and was excluded once the pattern became `**/.vinext`), and
# the app's own `.vinext` lives at `apps/file-manager/.vinext` — one level
# below this file — so a bare line here would have compiled, looked correct,
# and silently done nothing. The same gap almost certainly affects several of
# the bare patterns already above this comment (`node_modules`, `.next`,
# `.turbo`, `dist`, `coverage`, `docs` all live nested under `apps/*` /
# `packages/*` too) — out of scope for #1284, flagged rather than fixed here
# so it isn't lost.
#
# Proved end-to-end with a real `docker build` of the UNMODIFIED Dockerfile:
# WITHOUT this exclusion (even with the bare, non-recursive `.vinext` line),
# the served HTML still referenced the host checkout's own
# `.vinext/fonts/...` path (404s) — confirmed by exec'ing into the builder
# stage and finding `/repo/apps/file-manager/.vinext` present with the HOST's
# absolute path baked into its cached style.css. WITH the `**/` prefix, that
# directory does not reach the builder stage at all, the in-image `vite
# build` fetches the font fresh, and every font reference in the served HTML
# resolved to `/_next/static/_vinext_fonts/...`, serving 200 `font/woff2`.
**/.vinext

# Same staleness class as `.vinext` above: `.output` is the HOST build's
# output tree. The Dockerfile runs its own `vite build` and does not read a
# pre-existing `.output`, so excluding it costs nothing and removes another
# host-build artifact from the context. Also needs the `**/` prefix for the
# same reason.
**/.output
